// Lesson 1.5 — Movement II: Speed, deltaTime & Tuning
// First-introduction lesson for the vector-length idea: FULL scaffold (level 1).
//
// WHAT CHANGED AND WHY (alignment pass, 2026-11-05): the old page taught
// `direction.normalized` as the fix the student ships. The built game does not
// normalize — Aram's ruling was "No need to add .normalized now" — so this page
// would have left every student with a file that no longer matched the project,
// and would have contradicted the diagonal-speed bug the class can actually
// feel in the game today.
//
// The lesson keeps the whole idea and changes the verb: the bug is MEASURED and
// the one-line fix is NAMED AND PARKED. That is deliberate, and it is the first
// time the course says out loud what Aram asked to say out loud — an MVP is
// allowed to be wrong in a way you can name, and coming back to fix it well is
// its own concept. The `.normalized` line appears in a "Known Debt" block, not
// in the reference file, so a student can always tell which of the two they are
// reading.
//
// THE CODE DELIVERABLE is small on purpose (small lessons, lots of catch-up
// time): the two axes move out of the movement line and into `xVector` /
// `yVector` fields, which 1.6 branches on and 2.2 hands to `linearVelocity`.
//
